{
  "class": "reference",
  "note": "Rung 3: a visitor can point back at something instead of naming it. Three cue kinds: ordinals ('the second one', resolved against the list the previous answer produced), demonstrative pronouns ('its stack', 'does that project use sqlite', resolved against the previous subject), and partial names ('ground' for Groundglass). Personal pronouns (he/his) are a person reference, not a project one, so they must never resolve to a project. Tasks with no context and no partial must resolve to nothing.",
  "subjects": [
    "Hobnob",
    "Readback",
    "Groundglass",
    "boaz",
    "Python 3.10+",
    "SQLite",
    "TypeScript",
    "the archive",
    "the blog",
    "the resume",
    "the assistant",
    "the site",
    "Conversica",
    "shobyde.com"
  ],
  "tasks": [
